# Cloudflare Pages — URL redirects
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Format: /from /to [status]   (301 default; 302 temporary; 200 rewrite)
#
# SPA routing is handled automatically: because the build output has no
# top-level 404.html, Cloudflare Pages treats this as a single-page app
# and serves index.html for any unmatched path, so deep links such as
# /product/<slug> resolve to the SPA shell and Angular routes client-side.
# Do NOT add a "/* /index.html 200" catch-all — Pages flags it as an
# infinite loop and ignores it. Also note: _redirects rules never apply
# to Pages Function routes, so /auth-proxy/* is unaffected.
#
# Real content redirects go here as URLs evolve, e.g.:
#   /home / 301
#   /old-slug /new-slug 301
